mometer reading? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality." :question/worked-solution "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={64}^{∘}\\text{F},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-64).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b80c3e-e59a-547b-a782-41612e4da31a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-67(T-145)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241227} {:answer/id #uuid "1ccf8a1b-29f1-5b0a-80ad-9958a78a6231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-145(T-67)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241422} {:answer/id #uuid "4f5e0f28-4de0-5f1e-ae81-d2cf901b0128" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-kT(T-67)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241889} {:answer/id #uuid "c6be0d3b-ed68-5a2f-af1a-64dc02f7559b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-67)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242933} {:answer/id #uuid "e362934b-110b-510b-8990-c6bccbecf578" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-145)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6be0d3b-ed68-5a2f-af1a-64dc02f7559b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-67)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242933} :answer-field/id #uuid "93430b60-75e1-51bd-a136-498bba75fcbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 1759218624