ferential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={35}^{∘}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-35).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "790823da-d3ca-5323-814f-de9286dc80bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=kT(T-70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672711} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e9d369-2677-5dfa-9910-3e1a09c8374c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=-k(T+70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672720} {:answer/id #uuid "ba0ad2af-a525-5d42-ab36-45c260029c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=-kT(T-70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672721} {:answer/id #uuid "cef92983-1935-54c2-bc91-99f0b03c7949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=-k(T-70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672724} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e1736e-a36a-5ccf-abb4-37d5783bd6f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=k(T-70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cef92983-1935-54c2-bc91-99f0b03c7949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=-k(T-70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672724} :answer-field/id #uuid "e15f2f6b-753f-59e6-83f9-114506d09104" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672726}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e423b9ad-3262-58aa-a896-09efb5972d47" :question/problem "The rate at which a freshly baked cake cools is proportional to the difference between its temperature and the temperature of its surroundings. Let $T(t)$ be the temperature of the cake in degrees Fahrenheit, and let $t>0$ be the time in minutes. If the temperature of the surround